title: The warped door
story: fernhill
continues: vine
description: The folly door will not open until Tobias has been made to talk
  about the fire. Ends the moment the door's draught lights the fuse — the
  branch point both fuse endings continue from.

---

# `on opening it while tobias is not shaken: refuse folly-jammed`. This is the
# story's own refusal, and it is only reachable by opening the door explicitly.
> open the folly door
[OK: contains "The warped door doesn't shift. Twenty years of weather have set it like a jaw"]

# The natural command gets the stock line instead — the story's refusal is
# bypassed by the phrasing a player is more likely to type.
> north
[OK: contains "The folly door is closed"]
[OK: not contains "Twenty years of weather"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Folly Hill]

> south
[OK: contains "Greenhouse"]

> east
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]

# The folly topic flips Tobias to `shaken` — the door's condition — and awards
# `truth worth 5`. Same reply as npcs.transcript; here it is load-bearing.
> ask tobias about the folly
[OK: contains "The door's only warped, not cursed. Shoulder it"]

> west
[OK: contains "Greenhouse"]

> north
[OK: contains "Folly Hill"]

# Same command as the first line of this file, opposite outcome.
> open the folly door
[OK: contains "You open the folly door"]
[EVENT: true, type="if.event.opened"]

# `after entering it, once` — the draught lights the fuse, and the sequence
# `when the fuse becomes lit` starts its three-turn count. Everything below
# this line is a race.
> north
[OK: contains "Folly"]
[OK: contains "a cache of ancient estate fireworks slumps against the far wall"]
[OK: contains "wakes a thread of sparks in the old blasting cord"]
[OK: contains "It is racing you"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Folly]
